"""gen_hong_kong_deep_dive.py — emits 696_hong_kong_deep_dive.sql.

Edit this file, not the SQL. Run:
    python3 gen_hong_kong_deep_dive.py > 696_hong_kong_deep_dive.sql

THREE THINGS THIS PAGE EXISTS TO SAY.

1. Hong Kong has no consumption tax, so it has no tax invoice, and the
   five empty headline boxes are a consequence rather than a gap. It is
   the first jurisdiction on this site with no VAT, GST or sales tax of
   any kind. A goods and services tax was consulted on in 2006 and
   dropped that December.

2. China's fully digitalised e-fapiao regime does NOT reach Hong Kong,
   and readers assume it does. The Measures for the Administration of
   Invoices bind persons acting 境内 -- within the territory -- and Basic
   Law art. 106 bars the Central People's Government from levying taxes
   in the HKSAR at all. STA Announcement 2024 No. 11, rolling e-fapiao
   out 全国, does not mention Hong Kong anywhere.

3. There IS one live mandatory electronic obligation and it is easy to
   miss between the noes: iXBRL profits tax return filing, phase one
   from 1 April 2026 for in-scope multinational groups. It is on the
   arrivals board. It is not e-reporting on this site's rule, because it
   carries accounts rather than invoice-level data -- and the page says
   both halves of that rather than leaving a reader to reconcile them.

ONE WORDING NOTE, FORCED BY A TEST. The vendor-error row first quoted
Thomson Reuters verbatim -- "B2G: e-Procurement System mandatory" --
and tests/guides-consistency.mjs refused the page: a fact row asserted a
duty the B2G tile denies. The check was right and rewording was the
fix, not an exemption. A sentence asserting a duty, sitting on the page
in quotable form, is exactly what gets lifted out of context; that is
how the phantom March 2026 Botswana mandate travelled. The row now
describes the claim instead of reproducing it.

The stat strip carries the absent rate, the profits tax rate and the
WTO accession year. Nothing in it restates a headline tile.
"""
